# siblings: the sibling checkouts each repository's gates reach as ../<dir> (read by aien-test worker).
#
# One line per sibling:  <repo> <dir> <source-repo> <ref>
#   <repo>         the repository under test (its trusted clone is <clones>/<repo>)
#   <dir>          the directory name tests/gates/run.sh expects next to the checkout (../<dir>)
#   <source-repo>  the trusted clone the sibling is made from (<clones>/<source-repo>, never the network)
#   <ref>          a branch of that clone's origin; the worker takes refs/remotes/origin/<ref> as the clone has
#                  it at run start and journals the commit (run.sh records it in the receipt as AIEN-OBS)
#
# This file is operator configuration, read from the trusted clone of aien-sovereign-core like wt.sh: a change
# under test can never choose its own siblings. Keep it in step with the need_sibling / pin calls in each
# repository's tests/gates/run.sh (LOCAL_VERIFICATION.md, "Sibling checkouts").
